Description: Point nixos-install at the flake staged in the target's /etc/nixos
 Upstream's nixosInstallCmd installs the generated configuration.nix on its own.
 --flake makes it evaluate the flake write-installed-flake.patch leaves there
 instead, and --no-channel-copy keeps a flake installation from dragging the
 medium's channels along.
 .
 The target store must copy outputs from the medium even when the machine has no
 configured network address. The nix CLI otherwise treats that state like
 --offline and turns substitution off, including substitution from the medium's
 local store. Explicit substitute=true keeps that local copy path enabled.
 always-allow-substitutes additionally covers outputs whose derivations disable
 substitution themselves. Keep both settings attached to the operation which
 needs them, across the second pkexec, instead of relying only on the medium's
 ambient nix.conf.
 .
 The output name is a constant because that flake has exactly one: it was
 written for this machine, moments ago, and names nothing else.
Forwarded: not-needed

diff --git a/modules/nixos/main.py b/modules/nixos/main.py
--- a/modules/nixos/main.py
+++ b/modules/nixos/main.py
@@ -1030,6 +1030,15 @@
     nixosInstallCmd.extend(
         [
             "nixos-install",
+            "--flake",
+            os.path.join(root_mount_point, "etc/nixos") + "#installed",
+            "--no-channel-copy",
+            "--option",
+            "substitute",
+            "true",
+            "--option",
+            "always-allow-substitutes",
+            "true",
             "--no-root-passwd",
             "--root",
             root_mount_point,
